  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "A rock band has $48$ songs, $\\frac{1}{4}$ of which are ballads. How many of the band's songs are not ballads?",
  "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of ballads to the total number of songs is $\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of ballads, and the denominator represents the total number of songs .\n\nWe can make a denominator of $48$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $12:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\times 12}{4\\times 12}=\\frac{12}{48}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the band has $12$ ballads. \n\nSo the number of songs that are not ballads is\n\n$$\n48-12=36.\n$$",
